# Copy this file to .env, in the pitwall repo, to give npm run dev a fixed token.
#
# PITWALL_TOKEN fixes the token: every run that uses it has the same one, so a
# tab that has it reconnects after every restart. But any page or script that
# ever saw it can drive every later run that uses it. Use this only on a
# single-user machine or for development.
#
# Only npm run dev reads this file, and only from the pitwall repo itself. The
# pitwall command (node dist/cli.js) never reads a .env: give it PITWALL_TOKEN
# in its environment instead.
#
# At least 32 characters from A-Z, a-z, 0-9, "-" and "_". To make one:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
#
# Left empty, as here, it counts as unset: npm run dev mints a new token every
# run, and says nothing about a fixed one.
PITWALL_TOKEN=
